# .env.example -- joosep personal workbench (*FR:Brunel*)
#
# Copy to `.env` beside docker-compose.yml, then `chmod 600 .env`.
# Owned by the host `dev` user. NEVER committed.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTHING IN THIS FILE IS REQUIRED FOR THE CONTAINER TO BOOT.
#
# An EMPTY .env -- or no .env at all -- is a valid, working first start
# (`env_file` is marked `required: false`). That is deliberate, not a
# convenience: the container comes up under-credentialled on purpose, and
# Joosep's own team provisions what it needs as its first real work. See
# FIRST-TASKS.md, which is seeded into ~/ inside the container.
#
# So the first-boot procedure is: copy this file, change nothing, start.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# DERIVED FROM THE COMPOSE `environment:` BLOCK, deliberately. Do NOT inherit
# apex's .env.example: it is neither a superset nor a subset of what apex
# actually consumes -- it carries a TUNNEL_TOKEN no service receives (a dead
# cloudflared-sidecar leftover) while omitting three variables that ride compose
# defaults. The compose file is the contract; this mirrors it.

# ── Added LATER, by Joosep's team, not by the PO up front ────────────────────

# GITHUB_TOKEN -- leave UNSET at first start.
#
# Creating this is task 1 for Joosep and his agents: a FINE-GRAINED PAT on his
# own account (JoosepM-565), resource owner Eesti-Raudtee, "Only select
# repositories" = HES-integration-tests + rumba, permissions Contents:Read-only
# + Metadata:Read-only, everything else No access.
#
# NOT the PO's org-wide PAT. The entrypoint writes this value into the container
# user's .bashrc in cleartext and that user IS Joosep -- which is correct only
# while the credential is his to hold.
#
# It must NOT carry: workflow scope, packages:write, admin, or write access to
# any default branch. HES-integration-tests accepts direct-to-main pushes with
# no PR history -- the absence of a guardrail is not permission. He is not in
# `vjs-code-reviewers`, so the team cannot approve merges and must not be handed
# a path that lets it.
#
# TO ADD IT LATER WITHOUT A REBUILD: uncomment, paste, then `./joosep.sh restart`.
# That is `up -d --force-recreate`; compose re-reads .env only on a recreate,
# NOT on a plain `docker restart`. The repos clone automatically on that boot.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=github_pat_...

# ── Optional (compose defaults are correct for RC) ───────────────────────────

# Leave BLANK to use OAuth at first run -- recommended, and the standard here.
# He already holds a Claude licence and group (ITSD-39589 / ITSD-39591); reuse
# rather than requesting a new one. Credentials land in the joosep_home volume
# and survive restarts and rebuilds.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Git attribution inside the container.
GIT_USER_NAME=Joosep Madar
GIT_USER_EMAIL=joosep.madar@evr.ee

# Team name -- used for TEAM_NAME, the tmux session, and ~/.claude/teams/<name>/.
# Cheap to change later: volumes are named for the PERSON, so a rename is a
# directory `mv` inside joosep_home, not a volume migration.
TEAM_NAME=paunvere

# Repo overrides -- only if pointing at a fork or mirror.
# REPO_1_URL=https://github.com/Eesti-Raudtee/HES-integration-tests.git
# REPO_2_URL=https://github.com/Eesti-Raudtee/rumba.git

# ── Deliberately ABSENT -- do not add ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ATLASSIAN_EMAIL / ATLASSIAN_API_TOKEN / ATLASSIAN_BASE_URL
#   Atlassian access is the EVR CONNECTOR, authenticated interactively by Joosep
#   at first run (FIRST-TASKS.md task 2). It covers Jira AND Confluence under
#   his own account. There is deliberately no Atlassian secret anywhere in this
#   container -- nothing on disk, nothing in .bashrc, nothing to leak. An
#   earlier draft used a local Jira-only MCP server driven by these vars; the
#   connector replaced it and closed the Confluence gap in the same stroke.
#   Do not reintroduce them.
#
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN / CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID
#   VJS2 releases to Cloudflare Pages via GitFlow with PR review as the approval
#   gate. This team observes and reports on that gate; it must not be able to
#   pass through it.
#
# Any HES_ / VJS_ / PONY_ test-user secret
#   The shared root .env holds live test-user secrets on a shared account. Keep
#   it out of this container entirely.
#
# Any endpoint URL for the Elron/PONY message tooling
#   That tooling can emit into a LIVE railway dispatch system. Commit 39f16a83
#   (2026-08-26) removed the `isTest` toggle and the server now always sends
#   isTest=false, so a flag-based guardrail no longer exists. The as-built
#   guardrail is TEST-ENDPOINT-ONLY ROUTING, and it holds ONLY while the
#   endpoint is not configurable from inside the container -- which means never
#   putting it in this file. Do not reference `isTest` anywhere.
